Explanation of Position at the adoption of the Resolution entitled, “The role of Artificial Intelligence in creating new opportunities for sustainable development in Central Asia.”
Jonathan Shrier
Acting Representative to the UN Economic and Social Council
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President. The United States appreciates Tajikistan’s leadership and collaboration on this important topic.
A deep concern we have about this resolution is its reaffirmation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).
The 2030 Agenda and the SDGs advance a program of soft global governance that is inconsistent with U.S. sovereignty and adverse to the rights and interests of Americans.
We regret the endorsement of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development included in this resolution.
The United States rejects and denounces the 2030 Agenda and will no longer reaffirm the SDGs as a matter of course.
As such, the United States disassociates from preambular paragraph two.
Additionally, although we strongly support the general idea of capacity building in the field of artificial intelligence, we believe a Dushanbe artificial intelligence center would be duplicative to other development centers which already exist in the region.
Therefore, we do not support any such center and will not support any associated costs related to it. Thank you.
