Explanation of Position at the adoption of the International Day for Awareness of Landlocked Developing Countries Special Development Needs and Challenges
Jonathan Shrier
Acting Representative to the UN Economic and Social Council
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President, and the United States also appreciates Bolivia and Turkmenistan’s efforts to draw attention to the complex challenges facing the Landlocked Developing Countries.
We appreciate Turkmenistan’s hosting of the upcoming LLDC3 conference and look forward to sending our delegation to Awaza.
However, this resolution contains positions that the United States cannot support and so we must dissociate from this resolution in its entirety. As we have expressed previously, the United States will no longer reaffirm the 2030 Agenda as a matter of course.
This resolution also contributes to the proliferation of theme days, many of which have a similar purpose.
Thank you.
